    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Question\n\nI'm currently in the process of moving from vim-sandwich to mini.surround. My first impression is very good; thanks!\r\n\r\nOne minor, but still substantial, difference is that I had vim-sandwich set up so that when I did a dot-repeat, it would not move my cursor. This feels much more natural to me, and I'm curious if it is possible to get the same behaviour in mini.surround?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.surround</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm currently in the process of moving from vim-sandwich to mini.surround. My first impression is very good; thanks!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">One minor, but still substantial, difference is that I had vim-sandwich set up so that when I did a dot-repeat, it would not move my cursor. This feels much more natural to me, and I'm curious if it is possible to get the same behaviour in mini.surround?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.surround\nQuestion\nI'm currently in the process of moving from vim-sandwich to mini.surround. My first impression is very good; thanks!\nOne minor, but still substantial, difference is that I had vim-sandwich set up so that when I did a dot-repeat, it would not move my cursor. This feels much more natural to me, and I'm curious if it is possible to get the same behaviour in mini.surround?",
