                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Code complexity does play a big part in the decision, but mostly it is motivated by the fact that moving cursor to the start of the operated region is how built-in operators work. This is used as motivation for other modules that provide operators.\r\n\r\nStrictly, speaking, `sd` and `sr` are not \"operators\" per se (they don't require a textobject/motion after them), but I think they are close enough (require surrounding id and are dot-repeatable) to also behave by these rules.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Code complexity does play a big part in the decision, but mostly it is motivated by the fact that moving cursor to the start of the operated region is how built-in operators work. This is used as motivation for other modules that provide operators.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Strictly, speaking, <code class=\"notranslate\">sd</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">sr</code> are not \"operators\" per se (they don't require a textobject/motion after them), but I think they are close enough (require surrounding id and are dot-repeatable) to also behave by these rules.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Code complexity does play a big part in the decision, but mostly it is motivated by the fact that moving cursor to the start of the operated region is how built-in operators work. This is used as motivation for other modules that provide operators.\nStrictly, speaking, sd and sr are not \"operators\" per se (they don't require a textobject/motion after them), but I think they are close enough (require surrounding id and are dot-repeatable) to also behave by these rules.",
